From: virus1999 <virus1999@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: declare ppe flow stats helper before use

9999-15-net-airoha-report-unsupported-ppe-flow-stats.patch calls
airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available() inside airoha_ppe_debugfs_foe_show(),
while the static definition lives further down the same file. GCC 14+
turns the resulting implicit declaration into an error and then rejects
the definition as a conflicting type, so target/linux fails to build.

Add a forward declaration right after the includes.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c
@@ -9,2 +9,10 @@
 #include "airoha_regs.h"
 #include "airoha_eth.h"
+/*
+ * airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available() is first used in
+ * airoha_ppe_debugfs_foe_show() but its definition lives further down the
+ * file. Add a forward declaration so the call sees the real prototype
+ * instead of an implicit int, and the definition below does not conflict.
+ */
+static bool airoha_ppe_flow_stats_available(struct airoha_ppe *ppe);
+
